# JS/TS files are formatted by ESLint (@stylistic) — not Prettier.
# Prettier handles JSON, YAML, CSS, and Markdown only.
# (All JS/TS/JSX/TSX variants are listed so the per-package `prettier --write .`
#  — which scopes via this ignore file, not an extension glob — stays off them.)
*.cjs
*.cts
*.js
*.jsx
*.mjs
*.mts
*.ts
*.tsx

# Component SFCs, for exactly the same reason — Prettier claims `.vue` out of the box. The two genuinely disagree: Prettier
# writes `{ required: [...values] }` where `@stylistic/object-curly-spacing` (as configured
# here) wants `{ required: [...values]}`, so `pnpm prettier:fix` and `pnpm lint` would undo
# each other forever on any Vue file. `.svelte` is listed pre-emptively: Prettier does not
# claim it only because `prettier-plugin-svelte` is not installed, which is a
# dependency away from becoming the same bug.
*.svelte
*.vue

# Lockfiles — managed by package manager, never reformat
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml

# The workspace manifest — hand-authored, and Prettier fights the author over it.
#
# Prettier rewrites single-quoted YAML scalars to double quotes, so every `overrides:` entry and the
# `@parcel/watcher` key churn the moment anyone touches this file for an unrelated reason: a few
# lines of comment arrive as a whole-file diff in the file that carries the repo's supply-chain
# policy, and reviewing a policy change means reading past dozens of quote flips.
#
# Single and double quotes are equivalent in YAML for every value here (no escapes, no leading
# sigils), so there is nothing to gain and a reviewable diff to lose.
pnpm-workspace.yaml

# The local pnpm content-addressable store.
#
# 🔴 The `prettier:check` script globs `**/*.{...,json,...}` and the store holds ~900 package
# manifests, so without this entry the run reports hundreds of files that are not this repo's — output
# nobody can read, which hides real findings in tracked sources. A gate whose output cannot be read is
# not a gate.
.pnpm-store/

# Generated framework output and transient run artifacts. `.svelte-kit/` is regenerated by
# `svelte-kit sync` on every install and dev boot, so formatting it is both pointless and lost.
**/.svelte-kit/
tmp/
test-results/
.coverage-probe/

# Build output (generated — never format). SvelteKit's adapter writes to `build/`, not `dist/`.
**/dist/
**/build/
**/coverage/
**/.turbo/

# The wine FULL corpus, as linked into each vertical's static directory.
#
# `pnpm link:wine-corpus` puts a 116 MB `data-real-full.json` in every vertical. Five of them are
# symlinks, which Prettier refuses by design ("Explicitly specified pattern ... is a symbolic
# link") — so this never mattered. **Angular's is a HARD link**, because `@angular/build`'s dev
# server will not serve a symlink from `public/` at all, and a hard link is
# indistinguishable from a real file to every tool including this one.
#
# `.json` is a format Prettier parses, so without these globs `prettier --write .` in that package
# loads 116 MB into the V8 heap and dies — `Abort trap: 6`, surfacing as
# `examples-angular#lint:fix exited (134)` with no filename anywhere in the output. The corpus LIVES in the engine repository's
# `packages/mock-data`, whose own ignore file covers it there; these globs cover where it is linked to.
#
# `.ndjson` is not a format Prettier claims, so `--ignore-unknown` already skips it; it is matched
# here anyway rather than relying on that, since the glob costs nothing and the reasoning would
# have to be rediscovered otherwise.
**/public/data-real-full.*
**/static/data-real-full.*

# Angular CLI build cache
**/.angular/

# Verbatim license texts — legal instruments that must match their canonical upstream form
# byte for byte. Never reformat these.
#
# 🔴 `LICENSE.md` IS the verbatim Apache-2.0 text. Without this entry Prettier would reflow it on the
# next commit that touched it, silently. `tests/tooling/licenseDeclarations.test.ts` requires it.
LICENSE.md
